DESCRIPTION

    SQLite is an embeddable SQL relational database with a ~1mb
    footprint and a wide variety of features.

ORIGIN

    https://www.sqlite.org/2026/sqlite-amalgamation-3530300.zip
    sha256 646421e12aac110282ef8cc68f1a62d4bb15fc7b8f09da0b53e29ee690500431

    https://www.sqlite.org/2026/sqlite-src-3530300.zip
    sha256 bb80bf8a3bffc19241ce8aba5a4bc74e9c3980013cb0b5f0f0976a99516942af
    (only ext/misc/zipfile.c, linked into the library for the lua
    zipfile() binding)

    version 3.53.3 (2026-06-26)

LICENSE

    Public Domain or MIT

VENDORING

    the upstream two-file amalgamation (sqlite3.c + sqlite3.h) plus
    shell.c is vendored verbatim, with mechanical include rewrites and
    a numbered patch stack applied on top; run update.sh to bump the
    version (it re-fetches, re-rewrites, and re-applies patches/).
    sqlite3.shell.c recompiles the amalgamation with the shell's larger
    feature define set. extensions.h is a handcrafted declaration for
    the zipfile extension consumed by tool/net/lsqlite3.c.

EXTRACTED UNITS

    extensions.c's kSqliteExtensions registry names every ext/misc
    extension linked into libsqlite3.a. Most are vendored not from the
    sqlite source tree but by extracting shell.c's own inlined copy:
    update.sh's extract_shell_unit() takes the bytes between shell.c's
    "Begin ext/misc/<name>.c" / "End ext/misc/<name>.c" markers, rewrites
    the commented-out `/* #include "sqlite3ext.h" */` to the repo path,
    and restores any commented-out typedef (the shell inliner comments
    out redeclarations that would collide with its own, e.g. series.c's
    `u8`). update.sh re-extracts every registry name found in
    extensions.c on each version bump -- a new batch needs no script
    edit -- except names listed in its SRC_TREE_UNITS, which are vendored
    straight from the sqlite source tree instead (today: zipfile, from
    sqlite-src's ext/misc/zipfile.c). tool/lua/test_sqlite_extensions.lua
    applies this same rule as an agreement ratchet, so a version bump
    that moves shell.c without re-extracting fails there instead of
    silently shipping a stale unit.

LOCAL CHANGES

    mechanical (update.sh):
  - Rewrote includes of vendored deps (sqlite3.h, zlib, linenoise) to
    full repo paths for the build's dependency scanner
  - Replaced quoted includes of never-vendored files (windows sdk, tcl
    test harness, autoconf config header) with #error

    patches/0001 (sqlite3.c):
  - Enabled pread()/pwrite() and mmap I/O under __COSMOPOLITAN__
  - F2FS batch atomic writes use linux/f2fs.h magnums, runtime
    IsLinux() dispatch, and the correct ABORT_ATOMIC_WRITE ioctl
  - Use cosmo_mremap() for the portable mremap syscall pointer
  - Use arc4random_buf() so randomness works without /dev/urandom
  - Added msync() call to unixSync() for FlushViewOfFile() parity
  - Save and restore errno in some places to avoid strace pollution

    patches/0002 (shell.c):
  - Added /zip/.args file support to SQLite shell for white labeling
  - Load the symbol table when --strace is on so %t is symbolic
  - Clear errno after sqliterc processing
  - shell_stifle_history is a no-op (not in cosmo linenoise)
